\begin{abstract}
The principal new derivation extends the marked-line rank construction in
released family 252 from finite quotients to approximate permutation
models. A dimension-independent error certificate, a reconstructed finite
incidence argument, and a direct negative-curvature metric yield a
candidate torsion-free nonsofic word-hyperbolic group with a finite
two-dimensional CAT$(-1)$ classifying complex. The source construction is
credited; the robust permutation extension is the new step. A second
derivation gives a parameter-independent classical archive for one
correlated SU(2)-invariant Gibbs state with unknown field magnitude and
